[2026-05-31T15:19:42.326097] [INFO] Node Programmer Code Review - Event EventType.TOOL_CALL - Tool call read_file_segment for node Programmer Code Review Details: {'tool_result': {'path': 'arxiv_query.py', 'encoding': 'utf-8-sig', 'newline': '\r\n', 'start_line': 1, 'end_line': 36, 'line_count': 40, 'lines_returned': 36, 'total_lines': 36, 'snippet': '"""\r\nThis module handles querying the ArXiv database.\r\n"""\r\nimport requests\r\nimport pandas as pd\r\n\r\nclass ArxivQuery:\r\n    def __init__(self):\r\n        self.base_url = "http://export.arxiv.org/api/query?"\r\n\r\n    def search(self, query: str):\r\n        response = requests.get(self.base_url + f"search_query={query}")\r\n        if response.status_code == 200:\r\n            return response.text  # In a real implementation, parse the XML response\r\n        else:\r\n            raise Exception("Error querying ArXiv API")\r\n\r\n    def save_to_csv(self, results: str, filename: str):\r\n        # For demonstration, just saving the raw results; would parse in real case\r\n        with open(filename, \'w\') as file:\r\n            file.write(results)\r\n\r\n    def print_results(self, results: str):\r\n        print(results)  # Would format the output in a better way in a real case\r\n    def parse_results(self, xml_results: str):\r\n        # Parse the XML results and return structured data\r\n        # This is a placeholder for actual parsing logic that would extract information\r\n        import xml.etree.ElementTree as ET\r\n        root = ET.fromstring(xml_results)\r\n        entries = []\r\n        for entry in root.findall(\'{http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom}entry\'):\r\n            title = entry.find(\'{http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom}title\').text\r\n            id = entry.find(\'{http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom}id\').text\r\n            summary = entry.find(\'{http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom}summary\').text\r\n            entries.append({\'title\': title, \'id\': id, \'summary\': summary})\r\n        return entries\r\n', 'truncated': False, 'file_size': 1569, 'modified_ts': 1780233565.0843947, 'mode': 'line_range'}, 'tool_name': 'read_file_segment', 'success': True, 'result_size': 1927, 'arguments': {'path': 'arxiv_query.py', 'start_line': 1, 'line_count': 40}, 'stage': 'after'} Duration: 0.004794597625732422
