[2026-05-31T15:23:10.849108] [INFO] Node Chief Product Officer - Event EventType.TOOL_CALL - Tool call save_file for node Chief Product Officer Details: {'tool_result': None, 'tool_name': 'save_file', 'success': None, 'result_size': 0, 'arguments': {'path': 'docs/manual.md', 'content': '# ArXiv Query Tool User Manual\n\n## Introduction\nThe **ArXiv Query Tool** is designed to enhance the research process by providing flexible and time-sensitive search capabilities for the ArXiv database. Users can query the database efficiently and choose to either print the results to the console or save them to a specified CSV file.\n\n## Main Functions\n1. **Search Query**: Users can input search terms to query the ArXiv database for relevant papers.\n2. **Print Results**: The tool can display the search results directly in the console for immediate viewing.\n3. **Save to CSV**: Users have the option to save the query results to a CSV file for further analysis or record-keeping.\n\n## Installation Instructions\nTo set up the development environment for the ArXiv Query Tool, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Install Python**: Make sure you have Python 3.6 or higher installed on your system. You can download it from [python.org](https://www.python.org/downloads/).\n\n2. **Set Up a Virtual Environment**:\n   - Navigate to the project directory where the tool is located.\n   - Run the following command to create a virtual environment:\n     ```bash\n     python -m venv venv\n     ```\n   - Activate the virtual environment:\n     - On Windows:\n       ```bash\n       venv\\Scripts\\activate\n       ```\n     - On macOS/Linux:\n       ```bash\n       source venv/bin/activate\n       ```\n\n3. **Install Dependencies**: Use the following command to install the required Python packages:\n   ```bash\n   pip install -r requirements.txt\n   ```\n\n## How to Use the Tool\n1. **Run the Tool**: After setting up the environment, run the tool using the command:\n   ```bash\n   python arxiv_query_tool.py\n   ```\n\n2. **Input Your Search Query**: When prompted, enter your search terms to query the ArXiv database.\n\n3. **Select Output Method**: Choose whether you want to print the results to the console or save them to a CSV file:\n   - To print results, select the corresponding option.\n   - To save results, provide the desired file name (including .csv extension) when prompted.\n\n4. **View Results**: If you choose to print, the results will be displayed in the console. If you choose to save, check the specified CSV file for the output.\n\n## Conclusion\nThe ArXiv Query Tool is a powerful resource for researchers looking to quickly and efficiently access and analyze academic papers. By following this manual, users can easily set up and utilize the tool to enhance their research workflow.\n', 'encoding': 'utf-8', 'mode': 'overwrite'}, 'stage': 'before'} 
